  "limitations": [
    "TCP feedback is the last archived sample strictly before submission, not every native packet; receipt time and sample age define its availability. No future feedback is interpolated.",
    "submitted_monotonic is sampled immediately before submit_ordered. ServoJ windows identify endpoint candidates by time and recorded joint values; wire records have no delivery token.",
    "Client prediction time includes RPC and reply validation. Server inference_seconds sums all recorded draws. Their difference includes all work outside that timer.",
    "Submit-to-ACK and inter-block holds use host timestamps. ACK indicates endpoint RPC return; physical change is separately measured by the first archived feedback after ACK and before the next submission or StopMotion. These samples do not determine exact physical settle time.",
    "The fixed demonstration pickup is expressed in the initial cup frame, with tool0 TCP matching the flange. Submillimetre negative progress is numerical direction, not established physical error. Timing and direction comparisons alone do not establish a latency cause."
  ],
